<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shabdamanidarpana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shabdamanidarpana, &quot;jewel-mirror of grammar&quot;, is a grammar of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada language</a> written by the poet Kesiraja around 1260, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> period. Composed in verse with explanatory prose, it describes the literary language of the earlier Kannada poets. It remains the most authoritative classical grammar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-kannada">Old Kannada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shabdamanidarpana.jpg" alt="Shabdamanidarpana" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: fl. 1260 Kirja · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shabdamanidarpana.djvu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
